---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="35–45 min" data-extension-duration="10–15 min">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar · Lesson 02</p>
  <h1>Subject pronouns</h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Pronouns let us speak quickly without repeating names. Notice who is speaking, who is listening, and who we are talking about.</p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">≈ 35–45 min</span>
    <span class="tag">I / you / he / she / it</span>
    <span class="tag">noticing + tile drill</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Look at meaning before naming the rule.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Build the pattern from examples.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Drill</b><span>Repeat with quick feedback.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Personalize in short exchanges.</span></div>
  </div>

  <h2>What is a pronoun?</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>A <strong>pronoun</strong> is a small word that takes the place of a name or a thing.</p>
  <p>We use pronouns so we do not say the same name again and again.</p>
  <p><strong>Subject pronouns</strong> tell us <strong>who</strong> does the action, or <strong>who</strong> the sentence is about.</p>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Before and after</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><span class="ex">Maria is my sister. Maria is from Mexico.</span><br /><span class="ex">Maria is my sister. <strong>She</strong> is from Mexico.</span> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(She = my sister Maria)</span></li>
      <li><span class="ex">Tom is my brother. Tom is happy.</span><br /><span class="ex">Tom is my brother. <strong>He</strong> is happy.</span> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(He = my brother Tom)</span></li>
      <li><span class="ex">The book is blue. The book is new.</span><br /><span class="ex">The book is blue. <strong>It</strong> is new.</span> &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(It = the book)</span></li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <p>The second sentence is shorter and sounds more natural. The pronoun points back to the name.</p>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Name or noun</th><th>Pronoun</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>my sister, Maria</td><td><b>she</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td>my brother, Tom</td><td><b>he</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td>my sister and brother</td><td><b>they</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td>the book</td><td><b>it</b></td></tr>
      <tr><td>you and I</td><td><b>we</b></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. Use She for my sister Maria, He for my brother Tom, It for one book, and They for two people.">
    <h3>Quick practice: replace the name</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Tap the gap, then choose the pronoun that replaces the name</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="She">She</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="He">He</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="It">It</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="They">They</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Maria is my sister and a student. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="She" data-hint="The first sentence identifies Maria as my sister." data-fix="Use She for my sister Maria: She is from Mexico." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> is from Mexico.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Tom is my brother and my friend. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="He" data-hint="The first sentence identifies Tom as my brother." data-fix="Use He for my brother Tom: He is happy." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> is happy.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The book is blue. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="It" data-hint="The book is one thing." data-fix="Use It for one book: It is new." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> is new.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Maria and Tom are here. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="They" data-hint="Maria and Tom are two people we are talking about." data-fix="Use They for Maria and Tom: They are my friends." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> are my friends.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice the people</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Read the mini-dialogue. Before explaining anything, point to the speaker, the listener, and the people being talked about.</p>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Guided noticing</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">Ana: I’m Ana. You’re Leo. Maria is my coworker. She’s from Mexico. Tom is our manager. He’s in a meeting. We’re new employees.</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Who says <strong>I</strong>?</li>
      <li>Who is <strong>you</strong>?</li>
      <li>Which words replace names?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>The pattern</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Pronoun</th><th>Meaning</th><th>Quick example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>I</b></td><td>me, the speaker</td><td class="ex">I am a student.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>you</b></td><td>the listener, one or many people</td><td class="ex">You are my teacher.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>he</b></td><td>one person who uses he</td><td class="ex">Tom is my brother. He is a chef.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>she</b></td><td>one person who uses she</td><td class="ex">Ana is my sister. She is a doctor.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>it</b></td><td>one thing, place, situation, or animal when no personal pronoun is known</td><td class="ex">The phone is new. It is fast.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>we</b></td><td>me + one or more people</td><td class="ex">We are classmates.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>they</b></td><td>two or more; also one person when we do not know or need to say gender, or when the person uses they</td><td class="ex">My friends are here. They are early. · Someone called. They want a callback.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note-line"><span class="ex">They</span> can mean more than one person or one person. We still say <span class="ex">they are</span> and <span class="ex">they want</span>: <span class="ex">A new client is here. They are waiting.</span></p>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Sound natural: say the pronoun and verb as one piece</h3>
    <p>In a normal sentence, the pronoun is short and the new information is clear.</p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>sentence</th><th>natural rhythm</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>She is a doctor.</td><td>She’s a <b>DOC</b>tor.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>He is at work.</td><td>He’s at <b>WORK</b>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>They are from Brazil.</td><td>They’re from Bra<b>ZIL</b>.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Make the pronoun strong when you correct who: <span class="ex"><strong>SHE</strong> is the doctor, not <strong>HE</strong>.</span> Remember that <span class="ex">you</span> can mean one listener or many listeners; the situation tells us which meaning it has.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Memory move</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Point to yourself for <span class="ex">I</span>, to your listener for <span class="ex">you</span>, and to other people for <span class="ex">he, she,</span> or <span class="ex">they</span>.</li>
      <li>Notice the meaning first. Then name the pronoun.</li>
      <li>Practice <span class="ex">he / she / they</span> with the names of real people you know.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-answer-drill data-lesson-extension="Optional typed pronoun recall" data-success-message="Correct. Use she for a sister, he for a brother, it for one book, and they for two people.">
    <h3>Quick practice: choose the pronoun</h3>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Ana, my sister → <input class="answer-input" data-answer="she" data-hint="Ana is identified as my sister." data-fix="Type she: She is from Mexico." aria-label="Pronoun for my sister Ana"> is from Mexico.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Tom, my brother → <input class="answer-input" data-answer="he" data-hint="Tom is identified as my brother." data-fix="Type he: He is a student." aria-label="Pronoun for my brother Tom"> is a student.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>A book → <input class="answer-input" data-answer="it" data-hint="A book is one thing." data-fix="Type it: It is blue." aria-label="Pronoun for a book"> is blue.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Ana and Tom → <input class="answer-input" data-answer="they" data-hint="Ana and Tom are two people." data-fix="Type they: They are friends." aria-label="Pronoun for Ana and Tom"> are friends.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-answers>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-answers>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-game data-success-message="Correct. I names the speaker, you names the listener, we includes the speaker, they refers to others, and it refers to one thing.">
    <h3>Tile game: match the meaning</h3>
    <p>Click a pronoun tile, then click the matching meaning slot.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank">
      <button class="tile" data-tile="i">I</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="you">you</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="we">we</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="they">they</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="it">it</button>
    </div>
    <div class="slot-board">
      <button class="slot" data-slot="i" data-hint="The person speaking says this pronoun." data-fix="Match I with speaker." data-placeholder="speaker">speaker</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="you" data-hint="The speaker says this pronoun to the listener." data-fix="Match you with listener." data-placeholder="listener">listener</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="we" data-hint="This pronoun includes the speaker and other people." data-fix="Match we with me + others." data-placeholder="me + others">me + others</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="they" data-hint="This pronoun can point to two or more people or things." data-fix="Match they with two or more." data-placeholder="two or more">two or more</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="it" data-hint="This pronoun can point to one thing." data-fix="Match it with one thing." data-placeholder="one thing">one thing</button>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-tiles>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-tiles>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build it and drill it</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Now use the pronouns in real, everyday sentences. Each task gives quick feedback.</p>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. The context identifies she, he, it, we, and you; they can refer to parents or to one client whose gender is not known.">
    <h3>Drill: choose the right pronoun</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">Tap a gap, then choose the pronoun that fits the people or thing</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="You">You</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="He">He</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="She">She</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="It">It</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="We">We</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="They">They</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Sara is my sister and works in Berlin. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="She" data-hint="Sara is identified as my sister." data-fix="Use She for my sister Sara: She is an engineer." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> is an engineer.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>Mr. Diaz is my manager. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="He" data-hint="The title Mr. identifies the manager as a man." data-fix="Use He for Mr. Diaz: He is in a meeting." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> is in a meeting.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>This is my new phone. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="It" data-hint="The phone is one thing." data-fix="Use It for the phone: It is very fast." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> is very fast.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>My parents live in Italy. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="They" data-hint="My parents means two people I am talking about." data-fix="Use They for my parents: They are retired." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> are retired.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>My wife and I cook together. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="We" data-hint="My wife and I includes the speaker and one other person." data-fix="Use We because the group includes the speaker: We make dinner at seven." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> make dinner at seven.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>I am speaking to Daniel. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="You" data-hint="Use the listener pronoun when speaking directly to Daniel." data-fix="Use You for the listener: You are a great teacher." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> are a great teacher.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>A new client is here, but I do not know the person’s name or gender. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="They" data-hint="Use they for one person when gender is not known or relevant." data-fix="Use They for the new client: They are waiting in reception." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> are waiting in reception.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="she is a doctor" data-hint="Start with the subject pronoun She, then add is and the job." data-fix="Build: She is a doctor." data-success-message="Correct. She is the subject, so it comes before is a doctor.">
    <h3>Sentence builder: put the words in order</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Tap the words in order to make a correct sentence</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="a">a</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="she">She</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="doctor">doctor</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="is">is</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Your sentence appears here"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="they are from brazil" data-hint="Start with the plural subject pronoun They, then add are and the place." data-fix="Build: They are from Brazil." data-success-message="Correct. The word They is the subject, so it comes before are from Brazil.">
    <h3>Sentence builder: one more</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Tap the words in order to make a correct sentence</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="from">from</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="they">They</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="brazil">Brazil</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="are">are</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Your sentence appears here"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Spot the mistake</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Each sentence has one wrong word. Tap the word that is wrong.</p>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="she" data-hint="The sentence already has the subject My sister. Look for an unnecessary second subject." data-fix="My sister is a nurse." data-why="“My sister” is already the subject, so we do not add “she”.">
    <h3>Sentence 1</h3>
    <p class="ex">My sister she is a nurse.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="sister">sister</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="she" data-correct="true">she</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="nurse">nurse</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="he" data-hint="The second sentence points back to one thing: the book." data-fix="The book is heavy. It is old." data-why="A book is a thing, so we use “it”, not “he”.">
    <h3>Sentence 2</h3>
    <p class="ex">The book is heavy. He is old.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="book">book</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="he" data-correct="true">He</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="old">old</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="we" data-hint="The speaker is talking about Maria and Tom, not a group that includes the speaker." data-fix="They are my friends." data-why="Maria and Tom are other people, so we use “they”, not “we”.">
    <h3>Sentence 3</h3>
    <p class="ex">Maria and Tom are here. We are my friends.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="maria">Maria</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="we" data-correct="true">We</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="friends">friends</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Say it aloud</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Say each sentence with the correct pronoun, then reveal to check.</p>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Name to pronoun</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Say your sentence first, then tap reveal</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <div class="transform-cue"><b>Carlos, my uncle</b><span>→ ___ is a chef.</span></div>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal</button>
        <div class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>He</strong> is a chef.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <div class="transform-cue"><b>My mother</b><span>→ ___ is kind.</span></div>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal</button>
        <div class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>She</strong> is kind.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <div class="transform-cue"><b>The dogs</b><span>→ ___ are hungry.</span></div>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal</button>
        <div class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>They</strong> are hungry.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <div class="transform-cue"><b>My team and I</b><span>→ ___ work hard.</span></div>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal</button>
        <div class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>We</strong> work hard.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Quick check</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Excellent. You used the stated person or thing to choose she, it, we, and they, including they for one caller whose gender is unknown.">
    <h3>Choose the correct pronoun</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="she" data-hint="Anna is identified as my sister." data-fix="Use She for my sister Anna: She is from Spain.">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. Anna is my sister and my friend. ___ is from Spain.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options">
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="he" data-value-label-variant="case">He</button>
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="she" data-value-label-variant="case">She</button>
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="it" data-value-label-variant="case">It</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="it" data-hint="The car is one thing." data-fix="Use It for one car: It is fast.">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. Look at the car. ___ is fast.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options">
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="he" data-value-label-variant="case">He</button>
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="it" data-value-label-variant="case">It</button>
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="they" data-value-label-variant="case">They</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="we" data-hint="My brother and I includes the speaker." data-fix="Use We for a group that includes the speaker: We play basketball.">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. My brother and I are tall. ___ play basketball.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options">
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="we" data-value-label-variant="case">We</button>
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="they" data-value-label-variant="case">They</button>
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="you" data-value-label-variant="case">You</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="they" data-hint="Keys means more than one thing." data-fix="Use They for the keys: They are on the table.">
        <p class="quiz-question">4. These are my keys. ___ are on the table.</p>
        <div class="quiz-options">
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="it" data-value-label-variant="case">It</button>
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="they" data-value-label-variant="case">They</button>
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="he" data-value-label-variant="case">He</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="They want a callback." data-hint="The caller is a person, but the person’s gender is not known." data-fix="Use singular they without guessing gender: They want a callback.">
        <p class="quiz-question">5. A caller left a message, but you do not know the caller’s name or gender. Which sentence is best?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options">
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="They want a callback.">They want a callback.</button>
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It wants a callback.">It wants a callback.</button>
          <button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="He wants a callback.">He wants a callback.</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Communicate</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Pair drill:</b> point to people or objects in the room. Partner answers with a full sentence: <span class="ex">She is Maria. It is a pencil. We are students.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Personalization:</b> Write three true sentences using <span class="ex">I, you, we</span>, then read them aloud.</div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Quick self-check</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Can you say one true sentence about yourself with <span class="ex">I</span>?</li>
      <li>Can you talk about a friend with <span class="ex">he</span> or <span class="ex">she</span>?</li>
      <li>Can you talk about your family or team with <span class="ex">we</span> or <span class="ex">they</span>?</li>
      <li>Do you use <span class="ex">it</span> for a thing, not <span class="ex">he</span> or <span class="ex">she</span>?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Next use:</b> in your next class, introduce three people you know using <span class="ex">he</span>, <span class="ex">she</span>, and <span class="ex">they</span>. Then return to the <a href="#next-day-retrieval">five-minute retrieval check</a> without reviewing your notes first.</div>

  <section id="next-day-retrieval" data-lesson-extension="Five-minute next-day pronoun retrieval">
    <h2>Next-day retrieval</h2>
    <div class="lead-rule"></div>
    <p>Come back tomorrow. Try this short check before you look at the lesson again.</p>

    <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You retrieved He for a known brother, It for one laptop, and singular They for a visitor whose gender is not known.">
      <h3>Choose from memory</h3>
      <p class="choice-hint">Tap each gap, then choose the pronoun that fits the context</p>
      <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="He">He</button>
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="It">It</button>
        <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="They">They</button>
      </div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>Luis is my brother. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="He" data-hint="The first sentence identifies Luis as my brother." data-fix="Use He for my brother Luis: He is a chef." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> is a chef.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>This laptop is new. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="It" data-hint="A laptop is one thing." data-fix="Use It for one laptop: It is fast." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> is fast.</span></div>
      <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>A visitor called, but I do not know the visitor’s gender. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="They" data-hint="The visitor is one person whose gender is not known." data-fix="Use singular They for the visitor: They want to speak with you." data-placeholder="choose">choose</button> want to speak with you.</span></div>
      <div class="drill-actions">
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
      </div>
      <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
    </div>

    <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="we" data-hint="The speaker is talking about the parents, not a group that includes the speaker." data-fix="My parents are here. They are waiting outside." data-why="My parents are other people, so use they, not we.">
      <h3>Repair from memory</h3>
      <p class="ex">My parents are here. We are waiting outside.</p>
      <div class="spot-options">
        <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="parents">parents</button>
        <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="we" data-correct="true">We</button>
        <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="outside">outside</button>
      </div>
      <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
    </div>

    <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
      <h3>Say it without notes</h3>
      <p class="tile-target">Answer aloud, then reveal</p>
      <div class="transform-list">
        <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
          <div class="transform-cue"><b>Who is who?</b><span>I = the speaker. You = ___ . We = ___ .</span></div>
          <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal</button>
          <div class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>You</strong> = the listener. <strong>We</strong> = the speaker plus one or more people.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
          <div class="transform-cue"><b>Replace the words</b><span>My sister and brother are at work. ___ are busy.</span></div>
          <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal</button>
          <div class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>They</strong> are busy.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="prompt-card"><b>Thirty-second response:</b> identify yourself, your listener, one person whose pronoun you know, and one unknown caller. Use <span class="ex">I</span>, <span class="ex">you</span>, <span class="ex">he, she,</span> or <span class="ex">they</span>, and singular <span class="ex">they</span>.</div>
  </section>
